Terry

A couple of points in addition to those raised by Steve.  If your example is typical of your ability to resolve individual animals and their perpendicular distances, I would record individual animal distances and analyse your data not as "animals in clusters" but as individual animals.

This problem arises also for people studying primates in dense jungles, the groups are loose and it is a challenge both to assess a) the size of the group and b) the location of the group centre.

